  "_commit": {
    "id": "cbe969f207fa3888c910f9c0b6e91896d80a28f4",
    "author": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "committer": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "message": "feat: accept WKT-text geometry columns in st_join/st_join_table (0.99.9)\n\n.as_duckdb_table() (the in-memory materializer backing st_join/\nst_join_table's sf/data.frame support, added in 0.99.8) only accepted\nsfc or raw WKB geometry columns. MultiAssaySpatialExperiment's own\nidiomatic DataFrame shape stores geometry as WKT text instead, the same\nsingle-geometry shape .geom_to_sql() already parses, just never\ngeneralized to a whole column.\n\nAdded a character-column branch that parses via sf::st_as_sfc(), same\nidiom, scaled up. Along the way, found that st_as_sfc() errors outright\non NA (\"missing value where TRUE/FALSE needed\") rather than tolerating\nit the way the sfg/WKB paths do -- any WKT column with a missing\ngeometry would have crashed. Fixed by substituting\n\"GEOMETRYCOLLECTION EMPTY\" for NA entries first, matching the same\nnever-matches-anything semantics already used for the NULL-handling in\nthe WKB-list case.\n\nAdded regression tests for a working WKT column, a column with an NA\nentry, and genuinely unparseable WKT text. Full test suite: 0 failures.\n",
    "time": 1792598751
  },
